WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.500
In the past few years, many Republican governors

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.149
have signed legislation targeting 
LGBTQ people into law.

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:10.639
"Two controversial bills are now law in Alabama."

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:13.940
"A bill regulating what school bathroom Oklahoma
students use..."

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.930
"A house committee passed a bill 
focused on pronouns."

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:21.135
And hundreds more of these bills have
been introduced in state legislatures.

00:00:21.135 --> 00:00:24.245
More every year for the last 3 years.

00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:27.024
The laws are increasingly focused 
on what sports teams

00:00:27.024 --> 00:00:29.434
transgender school children can play on

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:33.876
which bathroom they can use,
and about the use of pronouns.

00:00:33.876 --> 00:00:36.381
But, these bills are at the state level.

00:00:36.381 --> 00:00:39.430
If you looked to the federal government,
you’d hear a different message

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.476
to transgender students.

00:00:41.476 --> 00:00:43.548
“We’re here to say that’s wrong."

00:00:43.548 --> 00:00:45.587
"And it’s against the law.”

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.620
That’s because the current federal government

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:53.540
believes gender identity discrimination
violates a 1972 federal civil rights law.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.260
So when it comes to the rights of trans students

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.461
conservative states and the federal government
are at odds.

00:01:00.461 --> 00:01:04.361
But the enforcers of education policy are
a third level of government:

00:01:04.361 --> 00:01:05.804
local school boards.

00:01:05.804 --> 00:01:09.689
And they’re caught in between. With 
extraordinarily high stakes.

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:15.127
I was thinking, wow, there's no way I'm ever
going to vote yes for this.

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:22.557
Gender affirmation is suicide prevention.

00:01:22.557 --> 00:01:26.100
This coming year will be my seventh year 
teaching in Tennessee.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.619
I'm seeing a lot more depression, 
a lot more anxiety.

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:35.261
I'm seeing a lot, a lot of suicidal ideation,
which the data bears out.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.789
One estimate says that 20% of 
trans and nonbinary youth

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:40.937
will attempt suicide.

00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:44.636
That's two times the rate 
of their cisgender peers.

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:47.109
And other surveys on mental health 
and trans youth

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:51.929
find that they are more than twice as likely
as cisgendered children to experience bullying

00:01:51.929 --> 00:01:55.039
or to not attend school because 
they didn’t feel safe.

00:01:55.039 --> 00:01:59.579
I do have a transgender son 
that is 17 years old.

00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:02.509
I live in Murfreesboro, Tennessee.

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:07.985
Almost nowhere have more anti-LGBTQ bills
been introduced this year than in Tennessee.

00:02:07.985 --> 00:02:13.470
And at least 2 anti-trans laws related to
participation in school sports and bathrooms

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.560
have already gone into effect.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.310
Tennessee’s bathroom law allows “students,
parents or teachers” to sue schools

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.635
if they “allow a transgender student in
the bathroom” of their gender identity

00:02:24.635 --> 00:02:26.480
“when others are in there.”

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.170
In our school, the rule is trans kids either
have to

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.410
use the restroom designated for 
their sex assigned at birth

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:39.455
or they need to go find a single-stall 
gender-neutral restroom.

00:02:39.455 --> 00:02:42.600
And our campuses were not built that way.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.630
From one end of the school to the other,

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.890
upstairs on this end and downstairs on that...

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:54.498
The one time that Toby decided to just go
ahead and go into the male facilities

00:02:54.498 --> 00:02:57.060
they started chanting.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.634
They started beating on the stall door.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:04.480
You're asking a kid to fight through dysphoria
and put themselves in harm's way.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.747
In 2021, when the Tennessee laws went into
effect,

00:03:07.747 --> 00:03:11.433
most school boards adopted it as policy.

00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.165
But not all of them.

00:03:13.165 --> 00:03:15.568
"We are being asked to pass a policy

00:03:15.568 --> 00:03:20.651
that goes along with state law, yet it is
a violation of civil rights."

00:03:20.651 --> 00:03:23.680
This is the Metro Nashville Public School board

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.460
which governs this school district of roughly
80,000 students

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:31.980
discussing whether or not to adopt the state
law that bans “transgender athletes from

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.760
participating in girls' sports"

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.300
"...in public, middle, and high schools."

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:41.490
"It is a moral and ethical dilemma for me as
a board member."

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:47.077
It was not something that anyone on our board
was willing to make the motion to pass.

00:03:47.077 --> 00:03:48.465
"The focus has just been wrong

00:03:48.465 --> 00:03:51.926
like how's this something that we're placing 
at the feet of our children?"

00:03:51.926 --> 00:03:55.542
"All those in favor of deferring policy 4.301
raise your hand."

00:03:55.542 --> 00:03:57.101
"Okay, unanimous."

00:03:57.101 --> 00:04:01.030
We're in this place now where we as a district
have been able to say:

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:07.291
There are adults and people in charge in your
life who support you and care about you.

00:04:07.291 --> 00:04:14.740
And so the thought that our hand may be forced
to implement these anti-trans policies is

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.494
very scary to me.

00:04:16.494 --> 00:04:23.179
But that decision is in a legal gray zone,
and it could have consequences.

00:04:23.179 --> 00:04:28.540
School boards, states and the federal government
all play a role in US education policy.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.872
But states in particular have the most power
over public schools within their borders.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:39.669
That's because public education in this country
is traditionally funded by property taxes

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:44.067
which are not federal in nature, but
they're state and local based.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.105
School boards can set their own policy

00:04:46.105 --> 00:04:48.810
but when states pass laws related to public schools

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.860
they are obligated to adopt them.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.720
If they don’t, they risk...

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.940
Funding, funding, funding all the way.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:01.686
That's a threat that hangs over our heads
pretty consistently.

00:05:01.686 --> 00:05:05.735
And I mean, we can't function without that
funding.

00:05:05.735 --> 00:05:10.794
Typically, the vast majority of public school
funding comes from state and local governments.

00:05:10.794 --> 00:05:13.710
But a small portion does come from 
the federal government

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.279
mostly through programs related to equity.

00:05:16.279 --> 00:05:20.244
Like for students with disabilities 
and for students living in poverty.

00:05:20.244 --> 00:05:26.000
These kinds of resources augment what's
available from state and local funds.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.900
Even though this slice is small

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.949
any school that receives 
“federal financial assistance”

00:05:30.949 --> 00:05:32.866
is beholden to Title IX

00:05:32.866 --> 00:05:36.409
the 1972 federal civil rights law that, 
for 50 years,

00:05:36.409 --> 00:05:38.189
has ensured that there is no “discrimination”

00:05:38.189 --> 00:05:40.251
“on the basis of sex.”

00:05:40.251 --> 00:05:44.529
And for public schools, the federal agencies
that enforce Title IX compliance

00:05:44.529 --> 00:05:47.352
are tied to whoever is in the White House.

00:05:47.352 --> 00:05:52.441
And the past three administrations have differed
in their interpretation of Title IX.

00:05:52.441 --> 00:05:56.816
The Obama administration ruled
that it protects LGBTQ students.

00:05:56.816 --> 00:05:59.606
But the Trump administration reversed it.

00:05:59.606 --> 00:06:02.888
And the Biden administration restored it again.

00:06:02.888 --> 00:06:07.849
That’s why today, in 2022, it is a violation
of federal civil rights law

00:06:07.849 --> 00:06:11.467
to discriminate against LGBTQ students 
in public schools

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:15.539
which could make a school district liable
to a federal investigation

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:18.939
while some states, who control most school
funding,

00:06:18.939 --> 00:06:21.069
have passed laws contrary to that.

00:06:21.069 --> 00:06:24.319
So school districts have to figure out 
what to do.

00:06:24.319 --> 00:06:26.559
And so do the families of trans students.

00:06:27.172 --> 00:06:31.196
I would say it puts us in limbo because

00:06:31.196 --> 00:06:38.205
while we feel heard and appreciated 
by the local board

00:06:38.205 --> 00:06:44.069
the state is still saying that 
they're not welcome.

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.960
So what do you do?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.799
It makes all of us want to move.

00:06:48.799 --> 00:06:51.529
I get a little fuzzy about some of it

00:06:51.529 --> 00:06:56.251
because the federal law says 
that you cannot do this

00:06:56.251 --> 00:07:01.008
that that supersedes the state laws.

00:07:01.008 --> 00:07:09.330
But yet they still do it and then they cite
Governor Lee's bills as a reason to discriminate.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.889
In states like Tennessee, this legal limbo

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:15.740
could eventually be solved by a lawsuit or
federal civil rights investigation

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.180
that could overturn a state law.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.382
There is already a federal lawsuit on behalf
of a trans teen boy in Tennessee

00:07:22.382 --> 00:07:24.563
suing to play on the boys’ golf team.

00:07:24.563 --> 00:07:28.639
And there’s a federal lawsuit over Tennessee’s
bathroom law.

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:32.409
But those won’t necessarily change things
outside of Tennessee.

00:07:32.409 --> 00:07:34.860
The institution with the power to do that
nationally

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.659
and that could force harmony with federal,
state

00:07:37.659 --> 00:07:41.661
and local policy would be the Supreme Court.

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:45.740
But if those rulings don’t come out
in favor of trans students

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:48.229
the last line of defense will continue to
be

00:07:48.229 --> 00:07:50.249
those closest to them.

00:07:50.249 --> 00:07:53.599
Teachers are going to be a big part of saving
kids' lives.

00:07:53.599 --> 00:07:58.421
Depending on just how willing they are
to be supportive, to be affirming.

00:07:58.421 --> 00:08:03.699
School has always been that one place
where we can hopefully find somebody

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:08.084
who will love us and value us for who we are.

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:14.448
Is there anything else you'd like to add,
just about your personal experience?

00:08:14.448 --> 00:08:16.483
I could share one thing with you.

00:08:16.483 --> 00:08:17.793
I came across this.

00:08:17.793 --> 00:08:19.444
Last weekend was Pride.

00:08:19.444 --> 00:08:20.687
She was very excited.

00:08:20.687 --> 00:08:23.414
This is what she sees, right?

00:08:23.414 --> 00:08:24.278
There she is.

00:08:24.278 --> 00:08:27.819
And there's all these people
supporting the flag

00:08:27.819 --> 00:08:30.781
and they're, you know, giving her hearts 
and fireworks.

00:08:30.781 --> 00:08:35.771
And I'm so thankful that this is how she feels.

00:08:35.771 --> 00:08:41.310
I can't imagine that if she did end up going
to schools

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:44.880
or being put into a situation where 
she wasn't supported

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:48.996
and celebrated, that this would 
not be the case.

00:08:48.996 --> 00:08:51.791
I mean, this is clearly the world that you've
created for her.

00:08:51.791 --> 00:08:56.159
I am not very good at taking credit for things,
but I'm pretty proud.

